\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1.6}{\ignorespaces The phase noise between the LO and the AS beams causes noise. The sensitivity curve for A+ sets the limit on how much path length noise is acceptable between the AS and LO beams. The blue line shows sensitivity curve is shown in units of path length noise between the AS and LO beams, and the orange line shows the requirement of HRTS mirror motion. The table motion was modelled as $1/f$ noise.\relax }}{25}{figure.caption.39}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterhrtsrequirement}{{1.6}{25}{The phase noise between the LO and the AS beams causes noise. The sensitivity curve for A+ sets the limit on how much path length noise is acceptable between the AS and LO beams. The blue line shows sensitivity curve is shown in units of path length noise between the AS and LO beams, and the orange line shows the requirement of HRTS mirror motion. The table motion was modelled as $1/f$ noise.\relax }{figure.caption.39}{}}
